title: Standing-order worker re-runs the full Slack access check every 10 s for a live huddle (~36 calls/min)
updated_at: "2026-11-06T10:27:18Z"
---
Observed 06 Nov 16:30-17:25 #core-sync huddle: while the huddle was live and until the fire fetched, the worker repeated a cycle every 10 s of auth.test, bots.info, conversations.info, conversations.members, users.list (Grant evaluation) plus conversations.history: 278 cycles, ~1,660 Slack calls for one huddle (daemon.log egress audit tool=standing_order:so_314...:fire). Only conversations.history (has the root ended / notes-ready reply) changes on that timescale. users.list is Tier 2. Fine for one order in one channel; with several orders/channels this will hit rate limits and crowd out chat traffic. Fix (P4 reconciler/shared limiter scope): cheap state probe first (history/replies), run Grant.evaluate only when a transition needs it (fire creation, fetch, post) or cache the audited snapshot for a few minutes; back off the live-huddle poll (e.g. 30-60 s) since the observer wakes on room-ended/notes-ready events anyway. Test: a live huddle for N ticks makes no users.list/conversations.members calls beyond the first per window.